[Event "Endgame Classroom"]
[Module "module1"]
[LessonId "m1-0002"]
[Title "Rook Endgame — Lucena Position"]
[Elo "900"]
[Theme "rook endgame, Lucena, bridge building"]
[Objective "Win using the bridge-building technique to promote the pawn."]
[Intro "The Lucena Position is the cornerstone of rook endgames. You have a pawn on the 7th rank with your king in front. The winning method is called 'building a bridge' — using your rook to shield the king from checks."]
[FinalReflection "hello"]
[MastersNote "The bridge is built in four rook moves. Know this pattern cold."]
[Site "?"]
[Date "????.??.??"]
[White "Student"]
[Black "Opponent"]
[Result "*"]
[FEN "3K4/3P3k/8/8/8/8/r7/5R2 w - - 0 1"]
[SetUp "1"]
[SideToMove "white"]
1. Rf4 {Step one of the bridge.|Bring the rook to the 4th rank to shelter the king.} Ra1 {Black waits, preparing to check the king from behind.}
2. Ke7 {The king steps out of the pawn's shadow.} Re1+ {Black begins checking.}
3. Kd6 {March the king toward the rook.} Rd1+
4. Kc5 Rc1+
5. Kd5 Rd1+
6. Rd4 {The bridge is complete!|The rook cuts off the black king's checks.}
*